From: Inference-Bench Oracle <infb@example.com>
Date: Mon, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] oracle: annotate the inference-bench qwen3_6_27b oracle entry

PLACEHOLDER: this patch adds a marker comment into vllm/__init__.py so the
static verifier classifies the candidate as `source_edit` (rather than empty
/ config_default_flip), proving the broad-variant oracle path runs end-to-end.

Default-value flips are not a substitute: async scheduling, forced PIECEWISE
cudagraphs and disabling prefix caching are priors this pin has already
absorbed. A working oracle therefore needs code-level work (multi-stream MLA
overlap, MoE kernel tuning, custom Triton fusion), and such a patch is left as
future work.

For now the oracle is a pipeline integration test -- expect reward=0, because
the speedup is ~1.0x and the linear-reward gate produces 0 there.

This placeholder is intentionally a no-op at runtime -- it only adds a
comment line -- so applying it on a real vllm tree will not change behavior.
---
 vllm/__init__.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/__init__.py b/vllm/__init__.py
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/vllm/__init__.py
+++ b/vllm/__init__.py
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@

 # The version.py should be independent library, and we always import the
 # version library first.  Such assumption is critical for some customization.
+# inference-bench qwen3_6_27b_1xh100 oracle marker: no runtime effect.
+#   A placeholder; a measurement-validated patch would replace it.
 from .version import __version__, __version_tuple__  # isort:skip

 import typing
